{
  "description": "Index of the community build corpus: one file per build in this directory, named by `id`. Each build file records what is fitted where (journal slot key + module symbol), the module’s power priority when it is not 0, `on: false` when the author left a module unpowered, and the engineering the author declared (blueprint + grade, and the experimental effect where one is fitted). The fixed cargo hatch is omitted. `metrics` is what this library derives from the build **as fitted, with the declared engineering NOT applied** — every figure comes from stock module stats, so a build designed around an engineered power plant reads `withinBudget: false`. That is the contract, not a defect: it keeps the pinned numbers a pure function of the catalogues, and one that is cheap for a port to reach. The engineering is still real data and nearly all of it is applicable: `declaredEngineering` counts the entries, and every one survives `applyBlueprint` except the 14 that declare a recipe no registry offers on that module — recorded, with their counts, in `engineering-options.json` under `corpus.notOffered` and `corpus.notGrouped`. An implementation passes by fitting the same modules into the same slots and reproducing every figure to within 1e-5 (figures are rounded to 6 decimal places here; `cargoCapacity` and `weapons.count` are integers and must match exactly); `role` is derived from what is fitted and is only a label. The corpus covers every hull in the shipyard with 2 to 5 builds.",
